    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Given that $\\log_4 a=3$, find $\\log_4 a^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a&=4^3\\\\a^2&=(4^3)^2\\\\a^2&=4^6\\\\\\log_4 a^2&=6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Given that $\\log_2 a=5$, find $\\log_2 a^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a&=2^5\\\\a^3&=(2^5)^3\\\\a^3&=2^{15}\\\\\\log_2 a^3&=15\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Given that $\\log_3 a=10$, find $\\log_3 a^{\\frac12}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a&=3^{10}\\\\a^{\\frac12}&=(3^{10})^{\\frac12}\\\\a^{\\frac12}&=3^5\\\\\\log_3 a^{\\frac12}&=5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q6-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What do you notice about the above questions? Can you make and prove a conjecture?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p4-q6-d-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The exponent multiplies the logarithm: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\log_b(a^c)=c\\log_b a",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", for ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a>0,\\ b>0,\\ b\\ne1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p4-q6-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Write ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a=b^m",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; then ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "a^c=b^{mc}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so the logarithm is ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "mc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The answers are the given logarithms multiplied by the respective exponents. Conjecture: $\\log_b(a^c)=c\\log_b a$, where $a>0$, $b>0$ and $b\\ne1$.\n\nLet $m=\\log_b a$. Then\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=b^m\\\\a^c&=(b^m)^c\\\\a^c&=b^{mc}\\\\\\log_b(a^c)&=mc\\\\\\log_b(a^c)&=c\\log_b a\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 47
      }
    ]
  },
